            <ArticleTitle>Tuning Edge States in Strained-Layer InAs/GaInSb Quantum Spin Hall Insulators.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>056803</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1103/PhysRevLett.119.056803</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a class of quantum spin Hall insulators (QSHIs) in strained-layer InAs/GaInSb quantum wells, in which the bulk gaps are enhanced up to fivefold as compared to the binary InAs/GaSb QSHI. Remarkably, with consequently increasing edge velocity, the edge conductance at zero and applied magnetic fields manifests time reversal symmetry-protected properties consistent with the Z_{2} topological insulator. The InAs/GaInSb bilayers offer a much sought-after platform for future studies and applications of the QSHI.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
